{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790258195,"nonce":"H9PloS/EZdnkAtxr7CRMVabvMrY=","title":"Lua typer: reads the types do not follow hand out shaped values without escaping them","message":"Three holes in the escape machinery of crates/zyntax_lua/src/types.rs, each a miscompile on zylua at dea6d08b (lua5.4 is the reference):\n\n1. Dynamic-key reads. `t[name]` with a non-literal key, `o[name]` through a class's `__index`, `rawget(t, k)`, and `any[k]` through a receiver the types do not know return Any, but the field's Func or Shape never escaped. `ops[name](\"10\")` on `{inc = function(x) return x + 1 end}` printed 52987011530755 instead of 11; `obj[k].x = \"s\"` raised \"internal: a value of another kind stored into a shaped field\"; `obj[k].y = 2.5` left `obj.pos.y` typed nil, so `if y then` folded false.\n2. Enumeration. `pairs`/`next` (also `for k, v in next, t`, a `pairs` iterator held as a value, `pairs{...}`) handed a shape's function fields out untyped: `v(\"1\", \"2\")` on an `add` field printed 425201762306 instead of 3. `ipairs`, `table.unpack`, `table.remove`, `table.sort` read through `__index`. The brief's claim that a typed `__index` handler is reached with an integer key does not hold: every `__index` handler already escapes as a metamethod.\n3. Dynamic-key stores. `t[k] = 2.5` with k == \"y\" widened fields only when the shape escaped; on a non-escaping shape the slot kept Int and the store hook raised the kind error. A name that is no field (`t[j] = 7` with j == \"z\") read back typed nil.\n\nFix: `ShapeInfo.untyped_reads` (names / elements / through `__index`) marks what untyped reads reach; settle escapes what they may yield and follows `__index` tables; receivers the types do not know, and library readers held as values, reach every escaping shape. A dynamic string-key store joins into every field and a new `dyn_value`, which reads of names that are no field (and blind stores into escaping shapes) now include; lookups do not skip such a table's hash part.\n\nConformance: functions/dynamic_read_any, functions/dynamic_read_shape, tables/pairs_escape, tables/dynamic_key_store, metatables/ipairs_index.","files":null}]}